            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Ko 3",
            "review_text": "Mervyn33\nSingapore, Singapore353 contributions\n0\nGood Japanese restaurant in Japan Town HCMC\nNov 2018 • Friends\nThis trip to HCMC, I decided to try a different Japanese restaurant in the Japanese district in HCMC.\nThe view of the restaurant on the side lane from the main road of Le Thanh Ton was not grand like Sushi Hokkaido but they have four floors.\nWhile we were waiting for our foods a stream of Japanese expatriates as well as local and headed for the upper floors of the restaurant.\nThe menu .. covers the standard items in Japanese restaurant. Foods wise it is as authentic and good but Sushi Hokkaido have a little more varieties.\nThe ingredient were fresh and the fish were succulent and the beef Sabu Sabu was great .. love the soup.\nIn terms of pricing .. it was a bit cheaper than Sushi Hokkaido.\nThe staff were very friendly and helpful and a few of them can speaks English. \nComparing my last visit to Sushi Hokkaido at Pasteur ... the service here was better.\nRead more\nWritten November 18, 2018",
